  "result": "The gate passed on the first run, using 1 of the 6 allowed. It returned **OK** with 5 witnesses and 8 names, and it composes LVMC_11_30_140_B_o1 and LVMC_11_30_140_B_o2.\n\n**The rule** (`NRS_484B_287_1d.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** a pedestrian under the definition DEF-NRS-484A-165.\n- **When it applies:** the pedestrian is inside an intersection that at least one lane runs into, and neither LVMC_11_30_140_B_o1 nor LVMC_11_30_140_B_o2 applies to them.\n- **What it requires:** at every such intersection, if the pedestrian is moving diagonally, they must be inside a marked crosswalk. \"Diagonally\" means that for every lane entering the intersection, the motion is across the lane but not within the right-angle tolerance of perpendicular to it.\n- **Narrowings:** I declared none; the record's own readings were enough.\n\n**The witnesses** use a 20 m square intersection with four approach lanes (north, east, south, west) and a pedestrian walking at 1.4 m/s:\n\n| Scenario | Scene | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | heading north-east, no crosswalk | violated |\n| permit | walking east, along the east-west lanes | compliant |\n| idle | on a sidewalk outside the intersection | not applicable |\n| blind | as forbid, velocity masked | unknown |\n| branch_1 | north-east inside a marked diagonal crosswalk | compliant |\n\nThe north-east heading is (3/5, 4/5), which gives cosines of 0.8 and 0.6 against the lanes. Both sit well inside the 0.26–0.94 band that counts as diagonal.\n\nThe record left two choices open. I applied the duty at every intersection that matches, which follows from \"at each such observation\", and I quantified over regions of kind `lane` as the record names them.\n\nThe report is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
